    {
      "id": "t1106",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 770,
      "y": 2516,
      "width": 382.8,
      "height": 180.0,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "a0106",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 17742,
      "version": 1,
      "versionNonce": 34378,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1785400000000,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "an idea, a product, a feature, an enhancement, a thought,\na question, a comparison to another product or repo \u2014 or\nan issue or a complaint.\n\nTRIAGED into one of three routes:\n  NEW      \u2014 idea / feature / enhancement\n  PROBLEM  \u2014 issue / complaint / something broken\n  OUT      \u2014 a question about the product. answered from\n             product truth, NOT framed as new work.\n\ncaptured by interview, uploaded evidence, or a whiteboard\nsession. the two routes converge on the same output shape.",
      "fontSize": 12,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "an idea, a product, a feature, an enhancement, a thought,\na question, a comparison to another product or repo \u2014 or\nan issue or a complaint.\n\nTRIAGED into one of three routes:\n  NEW      \u2014 idea / feature / enhancement\n  PROBLEM  \u2014 issue / complaint / something broken\n  OUT      \u2014 a question about the product. answered from\n             product truth, NOT framed as new work.\n\ncaptured by interview, uploaded evidence, or a whiteboard\nsession. the two routes converge on the same output shape.",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "customData": {
        "gen": "kerd"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "t1107",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1190,
      "y": 2516,
      "width": 382.8,
      "height": 210.0,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "a0107",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 17749,
      "version": 1,
      "versionNonce": 34391,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1785400000000,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "PROBLEM route MUST read the CURRENT situation first \u2014\ncode, infra, product specs \u2014 and then do the gap analysis.\nno proposal before the present state is read.\n\nNEW route: the competitor scan, and the evidence of need.\nthere may be no current situation to read.\n\nsensei is a TOOL, not a MUST. invoked when its route\nmatches: asserting a position, proving a gap or an idea\nwith measurement, or a complex problem needing point of\ncause and 5 whys \u2014 triggered by a problem that survived\na few attempts to fix it. otherwise avoided.\nsame rule for superpowers and every other external tool:\nit declares the route it serves, and is invoked on match.",
      "fontSize": 12,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "PROBLEM route MUST read the CURRENT situation first \u2014\ncode, infra, product specs \u2014 and then do the gap analysis.\nno proposal before the present state is read.\n\nNEW route: the competitor scan, and the evidence of need.\nthere may be no current situation to read.\n\nsensei is a TOOL, not a MUST. invoked when its route\nmatches: asserting a position, proving a gap or an idea\nwith measurement, or a complex problem needing point of\ncause and 5 whys \u2014 triggered by a problem that survived\na few attempts to fix it. otherwise avoided.\nsame rule for superpowers and every other external tool:\nit declares the route it serves, and is invoked on match.",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "customData": {
        "gen": "kerd"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "t1108",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1610,
      "y": 2516,
      "width": 402.6,
      "height": 195.0,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "a0108",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 17756,
      "version": 1,
      "versionNonce": 34404,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1785400000000,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "TWO documents, not one shape with optional sections.\nboth are a .md \u2014 machine-read, long-read, measurable,\nhandoff-ready \u2014 AND a diagram. the SECTIONS differ,\nnot the artifact types.\n\nIDEA BRIEF: what it is \u00b7 what it must become \u00b7 what gap\nit addresses \u00b7 how it compares to other products \u00b7 its\nvalue \u00b7 a viability SIGNAL, not a verdict \u00b7 next inputs.\n\nPROBLEM STATEMENT: what is happening now, READ from code,\ninfra and specs, not assumed \u00b7 what should be happening \u00b7\nthe gap between them, MEASURED \u00b7 point of cause, if the\nsensei trigger fired \u00b7 the value of closing it \u00b7 next inputs.",
      "fontSize": 12,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "TWO documents, not one shape with optional sections.\nboth are a .md \u2014 machine-read, long-read, measurable,\nhandoff-ready \u2014 AND a diagram. the SECTIONS differ,\nnot the artifact types.\n\nIDEA BRIEF: what it is \u00b7 what it must become \u00b7 what gap\nit addresses \u00b7 how it compares to other products \u00b7 its\nvalue \u00b7 a viability SIGNAL, not a verdict \u00b7 next inputs.\n\nPROBLEM STATEMENT: what is happening now, READ from code,\ninfra and specs, not assumed \u00b7 what should be happening \u00b7\nthe gap between them, MEASURED \u00b7 point of cause, if the\nsensei trigger fired \u00b7 the value of closing it \u00b7 next inputs.",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "customData": {
        "gen": "kerd"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "t1109",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 2030,
      "y": 2516,
      "width": 382.8,
      "height": 240.0,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "a0109",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 17763,
      "version": 1,
      "versionNonce": 34417,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1785400000000,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "TWO KEYS, neither sufficient alone. the routes converge\nhere: shared machinery, route-specific checklist.\n\nMACHINE: the sections are present \u2014 WHICH sections depends\non the route \u00b7 the measurements are stated \u00b7 the diagram\nconforms to the pattern it claims \u00b7 the next stage's\ndeclared inputs are all filled.\n\nHUMAN: Tony says approve.\n\nany gap or risk that could not be closed is documented\nAND confirmed. carried is fine \u2014 silent is not.\n\nHANDOFF: both routes go to Test viability. the killer\nassumption differs, the test does not \u2014 a problem going\nstraight to design is the jump-to-countermeasure failure.",
      "fontSize": 12,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "TWO KEYS, neither sufficient alone. the routes converge\nhere: shared machinery, route-specific checklist.\n\nMACHINE: the sections are present \u2014 WHICH sections depends\non the route \u00b7 the measurements are stated \u00b7 the diagram\nconforms to the pattern it claims \u00b7 the next stage's\ndeclared inputs are all filled.\n\nHUMAN: Tony says approve.\n\nany gap or risk that could not be closed is documented\nAND confirmed. carried is fine \u2014 silent is not.\n\nHANDOFF: both routes go to Test viability. the killer\nassumption differs, the test does not \u2014 a problem going\nstraight to design is the jump-to-countermeasure failure.",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "customData": {
        "gen": "kerd"
      }
    },
