    {
      "id": "t1114",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 770,
      "y": 2778,
      "width": 369.6,
      "height": 120.0,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "a0114",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 17798,
      "version": 1,
      "versionNonce": 34482,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1785400000000,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "the framed artifact \u2014 idea brief or problem statement \u2014\nits killer assumption, and the viability SIGNAL from\nframing. never a verdict; testing it is this rung's job.\n\nwhat counts as KILLER differs by route:\n  IDEA     \u2014 is the need real, and can we win?\n  PROBLEM  \u2014 is the cause correctly located, and is\n             closing the gap worth what it costs?",
      "fontSize": 12,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "the framed artifact \u2014 idea brief or problem statement \u2014\nits killer assumption, and the viability SIGNAL from\nframing. never a verdict; testing it is this rung's job.\n\nwhat counts as KILLER differs by route:\n  IDEA     \u2014 is the need real, and can we win?\n  PROBLEM  \u2014 is the cause correctly located, and is\n             closing the gap worth what it costs?",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "customData": {
        "gen": "kerd"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "t1115",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1190,
      "y": 2778,
      "width": 396.00000000000006,
      "height": 180.0,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "a0115",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 17805,
      "version": 1,
      "versionNonce": 34495,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1785400000000,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "risks are NOT unnamed \u2014 that was a drafted claim and it was\nwrong. they are unmitigated, unqualified, or accepted\nunknowns. UNQUALIFIED is the dangerous one: a named,\nunsized risk reads as managed because it is written down.\n\nEVIDENCE is what qualifies a risk \u2014 a TEST or an ANALYSIS,\nwhichever is cheaper and would actually change the decision.\nanalysis is evidence: not everything needs an experiment.\n\ntwo passes, or 'risk-driven' becomes a full risk register:\n  1. cheap estimate, to triage what could be fatal\n  2. real evidence for those candidates only",
      "fontSize": 12,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "risks are NOT unnamed \u2014 that was a drafted claim and it was\nwrong. they are unmitigated, unqualified, or accepted\nunknowns. UNQUALIFIED is the dangerous one: a named,\nunsized risk reads as managed because it is written down.\n\nEVIDENCE is what qualifies a risk \u2014 a TEST or an ANALYSIS,\nwhichever is cheaper and would actually change the decision.\nanalysis is evidence: not everything needs an experiment.\n\ntwo passes, or 'risk-driven' becomes a full risk register:\n  1. cheap estimate, to triage what could be fatal\n  2. real evidence for those candidates only",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "customData": {
        "gen": "kerd"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "t1116",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1610,
      "y": 2778,
      "width": 402.6,
      "height": 465.0,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "a0116",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 17812,
      "version": 1,
      "versionNonce": 34508,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1785400000000,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "QUALIFIED = proven AND measured. three fields, never one:\n  proven by   \u2014 the test or the analysis\n  impact      \u2014 measured, in the units VALUE was stated in\n  likelihood  \u2014 separately. do NOT multiply it by impact:\n                expected value is the wrong maths for a bet\n                taken once. 5% of ending it is not 5% damage.\n\nFATAL = impact >= the value framing declared, at any\nlikelihood. likelihood sets the RESPONSE, not the class.\n\nA RISK WITHOUT A COUNTERMEASURE IS A BLOCKER. that is the\ndefault, so silence STOPS the work rather than passing it.\neach risk therefore lands in one of three:\n  COUNTERMEASURE, PERMANENT \u2014 root cause addressed\n  COUNTERMEASURE, TEMPORARY \u2014 contained, not cured. carries\n    the condition that brings it back. an unmarked temporary\n    countermeasure is a permanent one by neglect.\n  BLOCKER \u2014 no countermeasure. clears ONLY by an explicit\n    act of acceptance: who, when, and on what basis. an\n    accepted UNKNOWN is a blocker accepted without even\n    knowing its size \u2014 allowed, but never by default.\n\nTHE LIMIT ON ACCEPTANCE: high impact + high likelihood +\nno countermeasure = DEAD PROJECT. not a kill you choose,\na state you recognise. every other blocker may be accepted\nby name; this one may not, or acceptance becomes an escape\nhatch for anything. only RESHAPE or KILL remain.\n\nverdict: proceed only when NO unaccepted blocker remains.\notherwise reshape, or kill. a kill here is a SUCCESS \u2014\nthe cheapest place the thing can die.",
      "fontSize": 12,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "QUALIFIED = proven AND measured. three fields, never one:\n  proven by   \u2014 the test or the analysis\n  impact      \u2014 measured, in the units VALUE was stated in\n  likelihood  \u2014 separately. do NOT multiply it by impact:\n                expected value is the wrong maths for a bet\n                taken once. 5% of ending it is not 5% damage.\n\nFATAL = impact >= the value framing declared, at any\nlikelihood. likelihood sets the RESPONSE, not the class.\n\nA RISK WITHOUT A COUNTERMEASURE IS A BLOCKER. that is the\ndefault, so silence STOPS the work rather than passing it.\neach risk therefore lands in one of three:\n  COUNTERMEASURE, PERMANENT \u2014 root cause addressed\n  COUNTERMEASURE, TEMPORARY \u2014 contained, not cured. carries\n    the condition that brings it back. an unmarked temporary\n    countermeasure is a permanent one by neglect.\n  BLOCKER \u2014 no countermeasure. clears ONLY by an explicit\n    act of acceptance: who, when, and on what basis. an\n    accepted UNKNOWN is a blocker accepted without even\n    knowing its size \u2014 allowed, but never by default.\n\nTHE LIMIT ON ACCEPTANCE: high impact + high likelihood +\nno countermeasure = DEAD PROJECT. not a kill you choose,\na state you recognise. every other blocker may be accepted\nby name; this one may not, or acceptance becomes an escape\nhatch for anything. only RESHAPE or KILL remain.\n\nverdict: proceed only when NO unaccepted blocker remains.\notherwise reshape, or kill. a kill here is a SUCCESS \u2014\nthe cheapest place the thing can die.",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "customData": {
        "gen": "kerd"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "t1117",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 2030,
      "y": 2778,
      "width": 389.40000000000003,
      "height": 210.0,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "a0117",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 17819,
      "version": 1,
      "versionNonce": 34521,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1785400000000,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "MACHINE: nothing is merely NAMED. every risk is proven,\nmeasured and given a likelihood, or is an explicit accepted\nunknown. impact and value are in comparable units. every\ncountermeasure states what it is expected to do \u2014 it is a\nhypothesis, so it must be checkable later. every TEMPORARY\ncountermeasure carries its return condition. no blocker is\nunaccepted.\n\nHUMAN: Tony accepts each blocker BY NAME \u2014 including the\nunknowns and any low-likelihood fatal. rounding a low\nprobability to zero silently is what this gate stops.\n\nan UNQUALIFIED risk reaching the next stage is the exact\nfailure this function exists to prevent.",
      "fontSize": 12,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "MACHINE: nothing is merely NAMED. every risk is proven,\nmeasured and given a likelihood, or is an explicit accepted\nunknown. impact and value are in comparable units. every\ncountermeasure states what it is expected to do \u2014 it is a\nhypothesis, so it must be checkable later. every TEMPORARY\ncountermeasure carries its return condition. no blocker is\nunaccepted.\n\nHUMAN: Tony accepts each blocker BY NAME \u2014 including the\nunknowns and any low-likelihood fatal. rounding a low\nprobability to zero silently is what this gate stops.\n\nan UNQUALIFIED risk reaching the next stage is the exact\nfailure this function exists to prevent.",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "customData": {
        "gen": "kerd"
      }
    },
