    {
      "id": "t1130",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 770,
      "y": 3362,
      "width": 382.8,
      "height": 120.0,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "a0130",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 17910,
      "version": 1,
      "versionNonce": 34690,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1785400000000,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "what is already built \u00b7 the framed and viability-tested\ncandidates \u00b7 their QUALIFIED risks with countermeasures\nattached, from Test viability \u00b7 and the record of what\nwas already ruled out.\n\nrisk arrives PRE-CHEWED. do not re-assess it here: a\nfeature carrying a TEMPORARY countermeasure is a different\nslicing candidate from one carrying a permanent fix.",
      "fontSize": 12,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "what is already built \u00b7 the framed and viability-tested\ncandidates \u00b7 their QUALIFIED risks with countermeasures\nattached, from Test viability \u00b7 and the record of what\nwas already ruled out.\n\nrisk arrives PRE-CHEWED. do not re-assess it here: a\nfeature carrying a TEMPORARY countermeasure is a different\nslicing candidate from one carrying a permanent fix.",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "customData": {
        "gen": "kerd"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "t1131",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1190,
      "y": 3362,
      "width": 376.20000000000005,
      "height": 210.0,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "a0131",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 17917,
      "version": 1,
      "versionNonce": 34703,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1785400000000,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "the five things that actually decide a grouping, and they\ndo not all work the same way:\n\nHARD CONSTRAINT \u2014 dependency. forbids groupings outright.\n  B cannot ship before A if B needs A. no trade-off.\n\nCEILING \u2014 how much change a user can absorb AT ONCE.\n  a release can be too big even when everything in it is\n  finished. almost nothing enforces this, which is why\n  'we shipped everything we had' is a real failure mode.\n  the bound comes from the RECEIVING side, not capacity.\n\nTRADE-OFFS \u2014 effort, risk, opportunity. these shape the\n  grouping among what is left, they do not forbid it.",
      "fontSize": 12,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "the five things that actually decide a grouping, and they\ndo not all work the same way:\n\nHARD CONSTRAINT \u2014 dependency. forbids groupings outright.\n  B cannot ship before A if B needs A. no trade-off.\n\nCEILING \u2014 how much change a user can absorb AT ONCE.\n  a release can be too big even when everything in it is\n  finished. almost nothing enforces this, which is why\n  'we shipped everything we had' is a real failure mode.\n  the bound comes from the RECEIVING side, not capacity.\n\nTRADE-OFFS \u2014 effort, risk, opportunity. these shape the\n  grouping among what is left, they do not forbid it.",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "customData": {
        "gen": "kerd"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "t1132",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1610,
      "y": 3362,
      "width": 389.40000000000003,
      "height": 270.0,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "a0132",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 17924,
      "version": 1,
      "versionNonce": 34716,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1785400000000,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "THE GROUPING. a release is a GROUPING, not a time axis \u2014\ntime may be attached later, or never. MVP / v1 / v1.2 are\nordered, not scheduled. conflating the two turns a\ngrouping decision into a deadline argument.\n\nTHE DONE CONDITION \u2014 assembled, never authored. every\nitem is a conformance check against an upstream\ndeclaration:\n  met the feature spec        <- the contract\n  met the product spec        <- the idea brief\n  goal of the function met    <- the goal set here\n  looks EXACTLY like design   <- design, approved pre-build\n  tests pass                  <- every proof layer declared\n     by Decide what proves it, INCLUDING user testing\n  documentation complete      <- DERIVED, not declared:\n     every declaration covered \u2014 feature, product and\n     problem specs, the changes and fixes implemented,\n     the solution diagrams, and what we ruled out",
      "fontSize": 12,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "THE GROUPING. a release is a GROUPING, not a time axis \u2014\ntime may be attached later, or never. MVP / v1 / v1.2 are\nordered, not scheduled. conflating the two turns a\ngrouping decision into a deadline argument.\n\nTHE DONE CONDITION \u2014 assembled, never authored. every\nitem is a conformance check against an upstream\ndeclaration:\n  met the feature spec        <- the contract\n  met the product spec        <- the idea brief\n  goal of the function met    <- the goal set here\n  looks EXACTLY like design   <- design, approved pre-build\n  tests pass                  <- every proof layer declared\n     by Decide what proves it, INCLUDING user testing\n  documentation complete      <- DERIVED, not declared:\n     every declaration covered \u2014 feature, product and\n     problem specs, the changes and fixes implemented,\n     the solution diagrams, and what we ruled out",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "customData": {
        "gen": "kerd"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "t1133",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 2030,
      "y": 3362,
      "width": 369.6,
      "height": 135.0,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "a0133",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 17931,
      "version": 1,
      "versionNonce": 34729,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1785400000000,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "MACHINE: every item in DONE points at a declaration that\nEXISTS. nothing in DONE that nothing declared \u2014 an\nunbacked item cannot be checked, so it passes by\nassertion, which is the unqualified-risk failure again.\ndependencies are satisfied by the ordering. the slice is\nwithin the comprehension ceiling.\n\nHUMAN: Tony approves the grouping \u2014 what is in, what is\ndeferred, and why this cut rather than another.",
      "fontSize": 12,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "MACHINE: every item in DONE points at a declaration that\nEXISTS. nothing in DONE that nothing declared \u2014 an\nunbacked item cannot be checked, so it passes by\nassertion, which is the unqualified-risk failure again.\ndependencies are satisfied by the ordering. the slice is\nwithin the comprehension ceiling.\n\nHUMAN: Tony approves the grouping \u2014 what is in, what is\ndeferred, and why this cut rather than another.",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "customData": {
        "gen": "kerd"
      }
    },
