    {
      "id": "t1148",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 770,
      "y": 3983,
      "width": 376.20000000000005,
      "height": 165.0,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "a0148",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 18036,
      "version": 1,
      "versionNonce": 34924,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1785400000000,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "stage 1's declarations, arriving together:\n\nthe INTENT DOCUMENT \u2014 idea brief or problem statement \u2014\nwith its MEASUREMENTS. those numbers are what the package\nmust answer, and what post-build conformance will measure\nagainst.\n\nthe QUALIFIED RISKS with countermeasures attached, from\nTest viability. a countermeasure is a CONSTRAINT on the\nshape \u2014 design builds around it, not a note in a document\nnobody opens.",
      "fontSize": 12,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "stage 1's declarations, arriving together:\n\nthe INTENT DOCUMENT \u2014 idea brief or problem statement \u2014\nwith its MEASUREMENTS. those numbers are what the package\nmust answer, and what post-build conformance will measure\nagainst.\n\nthe QUALIFIED RISKS with countermeasures attached, from\nTest viability. a countermeasure is a CONSTRAINT on the\nshape \u2014 design builds around it, not a note in a document\nnobody opens.",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "customData": {
        "gen": "kerd"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "t1149",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1190,
      "y": 3983,
      "width": 369.6,
      "height": 240.0,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "a0149",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 18043,
      "version": 1,
      "versionNonce": 34937,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1785400000000,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "read BEFORE proposing any approach:\n\nWHAT WE RULED OUT \u2014 so a dead option is not re-pitched.\n\nTHE ACTUAL CODE \u2014 not summaries. the 08-02 failure: a\nstale code comment trusted twice while the design doc\nholding the answer went unread.\n\nSTANDING DECISIONS \u2014 conventions already agreed that a\ndesign cannot violate. without them, settled ground gets\nre-litigated.\n\nLIVING DESIGN DOCS of whatever the work touches \u2014 the\nexact class whose retrieval failed on 08-02. the code\ncannot tell you WHY a neighbouring piece has its shape.\nsecond caller for reachability.",
      "fontSize": 12,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "read BEFORE proposing any approach:\n\nWHAT WE RULED OUT \u2014 so a dead option is not re-pitched.\n\nTHE ACTUAL CODE \u2014 not summaries. the 08-02 failure: a\nstale code comment trusted twice while the design doc\nholding the answer went unread.\n\nSTANDING DECISIONS \u2014 conventions already agreed that a\ndesign cannot violate. without them, settled ground gets\nre-litigated.\n\nLIVING DESIGN DOCS of whatever the work touches \u2014 the\nexact class whose retrieval failed on 08-02. the code\ncannot tell you WHY a neighbouring piece has its shape.\nsecond caller for reachability.",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "customData": {
        "gen": "kerd"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "t1150",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1610,
      "y": 3983,
      "width": 382.8,
      "height": 240.0,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "a0150",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 18050,
      "version": 1,
      "versionNonce": 34950,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1785400000000,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "ONE PACKAGE from ONE conversation \u2014 not four functions.\n(the draft split \u2014 shape / agree / prove / interface \u2014\nwas Claude's decomposition of the brainstorming checklist,\nnever Tony's shape.)\n\ndetailed specs \u00b7 architecture plans \u00b7 testing strategy \u00b7\nsolution diagrams \u00b7 flow diagrams \u00b7 visualizations for\nas many aspects as we can.\n\nat least TWO approaches with trade-offs before one is\nchosen \u2014 on constant axes, costs marked, bets named,\nresolved in ONE message.\n\nLIVES AT docs/design/<slug>.md + .excalidraw \u2014 living,\nundated, same slug as the product doc, so the pair is\nderivable. (chosen over folder-per-piece-of-work, 08-03.)",
      "fontSize": 12,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "ONE PACKAGE from ONE conversation \u2014 not four functions.\n(the draft split \u2014 shape / agree / prove / interface \u2014\nwas Claude's decomposition of the brainstorming checklist,\nnever Tony's shape.)\n\ndetailed specs \u00b7 architecture plans \u00b7 testing strategy \u00b7\nsolution diagrams \u00b7 flow diagrams \u00b7 visualizations for\nas many aspects as we can.\n\nat least TWO approaches with trade-offs before one is\nchosen \u2014 on constant axes, costs marked, bets named,\nresolved in ONE message.\n\nLIVES AT docs/design/<slug>.md + .excalidraw \u2014 living,\nundated, same slug as the product doc, so the pair is\nderivable. (chosen over folder-per-piece-of-work, 08-03.)",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "customData": {
        "gen": "kerd"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "t1151",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 2030,
      "y": 3983,
      "width": 382.8,
      "height": 210.0,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "a0151",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 18057,
      "version": 1,
      "versionNonce": 34963,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1785400000000,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "TWO KEYS, neither sufficient alone:\n\nHUMAN: every aspect Tony cares about is DRAWN, he has\nreviewed the drawings, and nothing is left to annotate.\n\nMACHINE: every measurement stage 1 declared has a NAMED\nANSWER in the package \u2014 point at where the design delivers\nit. the MEASURING itself is post-build conformance, not\nhere. nothing declared upstream goes unaddressed.\n\nGO writes a dated gate record \u2014 docs/gates/<date>-<slug>-\ndesign.md \u2014 and hands to CONTRACT (stage 3), where the\nscore is written. NEVER to writing-plans: the working\nhalf of brainstorming exits into the dead half today.",
      "fontSize": 12,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "TWO KEYS, neither sufficient alone:\n\nHUMAN: every aspect Tony cares about is DRAWN, he has\nreviewed the drawings, and nothing is left to annotate.\n\nMACHINE: every measurement stage 1 declared has a NAMED\nANSWER in the package \u2014 point at where the design delivers\nit. the MEASURING itself is post-build conformance, not\nhere. nothing declared upstream goes unaddressed.\n\nGO writes a dated gate record \u2014 docs/gates/<date>-<slug>-\ndesign.md \u2014 and hands to CONTRACT (stage 3), where the\nscore is written. NEVER to writing-plans: the working\nhalf of brainstorming exits into the dead half today.",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "customData": {
        "gen": "kerd"
      }
    },
