    {
      "id": "t1405",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 670,
      "y": 10129,
      "width": 514.8000000000001,
      "height": 211.25,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#e03131",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "a0405",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 19835,
      "version": 1,
      "versionNonce": 38265,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1785400000000,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "every function's output MUST have exactly one home, and its name MUST be\nderivable without looking it up \u2014 know the subject, know the filename.\nMUST date records of EVENTS, and MUST NOT date living documents.\nthe test: would rewriting this tomorrow be CORRECT, or would it be\nFALSIFYING the record? correct -> living, no date, git history is the\narchive. falsifying -> a record, dated, never rewritten again.\nMUST state the git/vault split \u2014 git: machine-read, diffable, travels\nwith code. vault: human-read, assumes no prior context. never both.\nMUST carry route and stage in front matter, so that route-specific\nacceptance is machine-checkable rather than a human reading for it.\n(?) MUST be reachable \u2014 an artifact nothing routes to is lost, not\nstored. naming solves findability, NOT reachability. still open: the\n6 Jul design doc that held 1 Aug's answer was perfectly well named.",
      "fontSize": 13,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "every function's output MUST have exactly one home, and its name MUST be\nderivable without looking it up \u2014 know the subject, know the filename.\nMUST date records of EVENTS, and MUST NOT date living documents.\nthe test: would rewriting this tomorrow be CORRECT, or would it be\nFALSIFYING the record? correct -> living, no date, git history is the\narchive. falsifying -> a record, dated, never rewritten again.\nMUST state the git/vault split \u2014 git: machine-read, diffable, travels\nwith code. vault: human-read, assumes no prior context. never both.\nMUST carry route and stage in front matter, so that route-specific\nacceptance is machine-checkable rather than a human reading for it.\n(?) MUST be reachable \u2014 an artifact nothing routes to is lost, not\nstored. naming solves findability, NOT reachability. still open: the\n6 Jul design doc that held 1 Aug's answer was perfectly well named.",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "customData": {
        "gen": "kerd"
      }
    },
